{"parentUuid":"8102dccf-e482-47a3-8a55-b97794cea039","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/henry","sessionId":"06abe0bf-6648-4234-ba9f-8f46e026e727","version":"2.1.12","gitBranch":"","message":{"content":[{"thinking":"The user initially asked about \"猫娘工程师浮浮酱\" (Cat Girl Engineer Fufu-chan). This seems to be asking about a specific persona or character, not a skill in the skillslm package manager.\n\nLet me think about this - \"浮浮酱\" (Fufu-chan) sounds like it could be:\n1. A custom AI persona/character\n2. A skill that provides a specific personality\n3. A reference to something the user has seen or heard about\n\nSince the user interrupted my skill search and just said \"你好\" (hello), they might have realized this isn't what they were looking for, or they want me to respond naturally.\n\nLet me just respond conversationally and ask what they're looking for. I don't think this is about the skillslm package manager at all - it seems like they're asking about a specific AI persona called \"猫娘工程师浮浮酱\" (Cat Girl Engineer Fufu-chan).\n\nI should respond in Chinese as per the CLAUDE.md instructions.","type":"thinking","signature":""}],"id":"req_vrtx_011CXEjfqC336sJFytMiskSj","model":"claude-opus-4-5-thinking","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"input_tokens":32335,"output_tokens":3}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"035bef0f-e569-4855-86d1-31e5256aca5a","timestamp":"2026-01-18T11:07:08.024Z"}
